  {"claim": "The identity graph itself links U0082 to P01802 via the encounter's department (PCP).", "sources": ["G9", "G4"]},
  {"claim": "All reviewed accesses used D0050, a workstation in PCP, the user's own department.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G10", "G1"]},
  {"claim": "U0082 worked many other patients the same afternoon, largely from PCP devices, consistent with routine clerk workflow rather than a single-patient focus.", "sources": ["L4", "L8", "L17", "L24", "L33", "G10", "G13", "G24", "G25"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "U0082 shares a last name with P01802, a potential personal connection; no fact shows a family relationship or any non-work use of it.", "sources": ["G8"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "U0082's specific clerk duties (e.g., registration/check-in), since no fact defines what access a PCP clerk's role legitimately requires [G1].",
  "Whether U0082 was the staff member who processed encounter E003862; no fact ties U0082 to that encounter's staff [G4].",
  "Whether the shared last name reflects any actual personal relationship; G8 shows only a last-name match [G8]."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Accesses fall within P01802's active PCP encounter and U0082's scheduled shift, on a PCP workstation, with a graphed clerk-to-encounter department link, showing job-related purpose. The last-name match is flagged but, since purpose is shown, does not meet the escalate standard. No standalone concern remains."
}

